  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "$$\n\nCalculate $\\int \\frac{2{e}^{2}}{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x$  for $|x|<1.$",
  "worked_solution": "The derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}\u2061x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2{e}^{2}}{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=2{e}^{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=2{e}^{2}\\operatorname{artanh}\u2061x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
